gDi(){return"Professional usage guide"},
gDh(){return"EndoDEX is a clinical tool designed to assist physicians in the structured evaluation of endometriosis. It does not replace clinical judgment or individualized patient assessment."},
gDo(){return"Purpose of the application"},
gDn(){return"The app integrates clinical history, rASRM classification, #Enzian classification and EFI into a single structured assessment. Its main value is to standardize information, improve communication between professionals and facilitate clinical documentation."},
gDa(){return"Clinical basis"},
gD9(){return"Endometriosis has anatomical, infiltrative, functional and reproductive manifestations. No single system fully describes the disease. For this reason, EndoDEX integrates complementary tools: rASRM for classical anatomical extent, #Enzian for deep infiltrating disease and EFI for post-surgical reproductive prognosis."},
gDx(){return"Workflow"},
gDw(){return"Suggested workflow: 1) Clinical history and symptoms. 2) rASRM. 3) #Enzian. 4) EFI, only when surgical evaluation exists. 5) Integrated results and PDF export. Each section can be reviewed independently, but full integration provides greater clinical value."},
gDs(){return"rASRM"},
gDr(){return"The rASRM classification is the most widely used staging system for endometriosis. It assigns points according to peritoneal implants, ovarian involvement, adhesions and posterior cul-de-sac obliteration. The total score defines stage I to IV. Its main use is to describe anatomical disease extent, although correlation with pain and infertility is limited."},
gDe(){return"#Enzian"},
gDc(){return"EFI"},
gDk(){return"Least Function Score (LFS)"},
gDj(){return"The Least Function Score (LFS) represents tubo-ovarian unit function. Tube, fimbria and ovary are evaluated on each side. Each structure is scored from 0 to 4: 0 = non-functional, 1 = severely impaired function, 2 = moderately impaired function, 3 = mildly impaired function, 4 = normal function. For each side, the lowest value among tube, fimbria and ovary is used; both sides are then added to obtain the total functional score."},
gDu(){return"Results"},
gDt(){return"The results screen integrates clinical information and classifications into a structured summary. It allows quick case review, visualization of rASRM, #Enzian and EFI, and PDF export. If sufficient surgical basis is not available, EFI should not be interpreted as valid and must not be used as a real prognostic estimate."},
gDq(){return"Clinical quiz"},
gDp(){return"The Quiz is a rapid simulator intended for training. Its purpose is to practice clinical reasoning and become familiar with the classifications. It has no real clinical value, does not replace medical evaluation and must not be used for decision-making in real patients. Every clinical case is unique and requires individualized assessment."},
